+The diagnosis is correct. At `5f6d3d5f`, the question was open with both stored replies marked acted (`5f6d3d5f:docs/user-feedback/questions/q-rstqvz.md:4-7`); the server removed them from `answers` and returned `waiting` (`5f6d3d5f:src/routes.ts:8762-8784`); their quotations were below `Details` (`q-rstqvz.md:24,40-50`), which the UI kept shut. A newly sent third reply would remain visible through `withLocal`; the started-at rule prevents older reads overwriting it, the pager only chooses navigation stops, retained questions preserve an open thread/draft, and the GET is `private, no-store` (`5f6d3d5f:src/routes.ts:9821-9823`). I found no separate ordinary disappearance path—only another agent acting on and deploying that reply, which is the same bug class.
+
+1. **P1 must fix — The rollback compatibility description is wrong.** The plan says a new client requesting `questions=3` from an old server receives shape 2 (`docs/plans/261010h-needs-a-decision-shows-replies-an-agent-acted-on.md:53-57`). In fact, the old route returns shape 2 only for the exact value `"2"`; every other value, including `"3"`, receives six-key shape 1 (`5f6d3d5f:src/routes.ts:9850-9857`). The new adapter must map both V1 and V2 directly to V3, with a test for each direction.
+
+2. **P1 must fix — `withLocal` must understand `actedAnswers`.** It currently deduplicates a receipt only against `question.answers`, then unconditionally changes the thread to `responded` (`src/web/FeedbackEarlier.tsx:649-668`). An idempotent retry can return a previously stored reply (`src/store/pg-feedback.ts:569-583`) while a list response already places that ID in `actedAnswers`; the client would then show it twice—acted and unacted—and incorrectly override `waiting` with `responded`. Deduplicate across both arrays, preserve the server state when every local receipt is already acted, and make the strict validator reject IDs appearing in both arrays (`src/web/FeedbackEarlier.tsx:377-396`).
+
+3. **P2 should — The proposed operating rule hides the current follow-up.** It says to put the new question “at the end of the body” (`docs/plans/261010h-needs-a-decision-shows-replies-an-agent-acted-on.md:82-86`), but everything after `Details` is collapsed (`src/feedback-question-values.ts:40-48`; `src/web/FeedbackEarlier.tsx:1514-1580`). That conflicts with the standing rule that the question and options above `Details` must be answerable alone (`docs/project/feedback-reports.md:515-528`). Better wording: set `answered` once Greg owes no further reply; unfinished implementation belongs in the queue. If a follow-up remains, rewrite the short section above `Details` to contain the current question, options, and recommendation; if it is materially different, close this question and open another.
+
+4. **P2 should — The proposed UI copy assumes every question has a `Details` section and that one agent recorded an action there.** The plan unconditionally says “what it did is at the end of Details” (`docs/plans/261010h-needs-a-decision-shows-replies-an-agent-acted-on.md:46-51`), while bodies without that separator are explicitly valid (`docs/project/feedback-reports.md:525-528`). Use conditional copy, or the more generally true “These replies were acted on; what happened next is recorded in the question.”
+
+5. **P2 should — The documentation and test scope needs to be explicit.** `feedback.md` is not optional: it currently specifies `questions=2`, unacted replies only, and says acted IDs never otherwise reach the browser (`docs/project/feedback.md:374-408`). The same now-stale contract appears in `src/feedback-question-values.ts:98-102`, `src/feedback-question.ts:17-20`, `src/routes.ts:8792-8802`, and `src/types.ts:7797-7821`. Tests should cover acted-reply bounds/order/count, exact V2 preservation, V1→V3 and V2→V3 mapping, strict validation including cross-array duplicate IDs, the `withLocal` retry case, optional `Details`, and the unchanged pager state. The plan also omits the required bug postmortem (`AGENTS.md:403-405`).
+
+**BUILD AFTER FIXES**
